artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $M$ be a closed manifold of even dimension $2m$, and let $\chi(M)$ denote its Euler characteristic. Recall that $M$ is said to be aspherical if its universal cover is contractible (equivalently, $\pi_k(M)=0$ for all $k\geq 2$). For a closed smooth Riemannian manifold, $\sec(M)$ denotes its sectional curvature function on 2-planes in tangent spaces, and inequalities such as $\sec(M)<0$, $\sec(M)\le 0$, $\sec(M)=0$, $\sec(M)\ge 0$, $\sec(M)>0$ are understood pointwise for all tangent 2-planes.

Prove or disprove the following statements:

(a) (Topological Hopf conjecture.) If $M$ is a closed aspherical topological manifold of even dimension $2m$, then
$$(-1)^m\,\chi(M)\;\ge\;0.$$

(b) (Riemannian Hopf conjectures.) If $M$ is a closed smooth manifold of even dimension $2m$ equipped with a Riemannian metric, then:
   (i) $(-1)^m\,\chi(M) > 0$ whenever $\sec(M)<0$;
   (ii) $(-1)^m\,\chi(M) \ge 0$ whenever $\sec(M)\le 0$;
   (iii) $\chi(M) = 0$ whenever $\sec(M)=0$;
   (iv) $\chi(M) \ge 0$ whenever $\sec(M)\ge 0$;
   (v) $\chi(M) > 0$ whenever $\sec(M)>0$.
